WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
 What's up, Marvel fans?

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.610
We're here with Kevin Feige.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.830
This is a huge
undertaking of a film.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.960
Where did you start?

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.490
 We started at
the ending of Far

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.230
From Home, where
we knew that we had

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.770
put Peter Parker in a very
hard circumstance where

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.390
his identity was revealed.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:18.420
And from there, we
decide what happens next.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.340
And how do we make
things harder for him?

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.760
He's been to space.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.550
He's become Spider-Man.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.050
He's lost his mentor.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.670
And now his identity
is revealed.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.100
And all he wants to do
is graduate high school

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.120
and go to college.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.530
And we started there.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.120
 And the good old
Parker luck kicked in.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.700
You brought supervillains in
from previous Spider-Man movies

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.500
into this.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.060
What was that process like?

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.390
 It was very emotional.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.840
It always starts with a place of
what do we think would be fun,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.410
what do we think would be cool.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:47.970
I've been making movies
for 20 years now at Marvel.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:51.090
And they started at this very
theater, as a matter of fact,

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.820
with the premiere of Sam
Raimi's Spider-Man 1.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.830
And we were sitting
around a room

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:59.160
and saying if I saw Willem
Dafoe, who you just talked to,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.950
as Green Goblin again and Alfred
Molina, who's not able to be

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.160
here tonight, as Doc Ock,
I would lose my mind,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:08.260
just that starting point.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.520
And a lot of luck came together
that they were interested.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.810
We were able to bring them back.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.110
 Oh that's incredible.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:16.560
I can't wait to see
this incredible film.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.750
What are you most
proud of throughout

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.160
the Spider-Man films?

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.080
 Well, I'm proud
of the collaboration

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.510
we've had with with Jon
Watts on three movies,

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.790
with Tom Holland on
three of his own movies

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.230
plus the Avengers movies.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:31.590
The entire relationship between
Sony and Marvel and Disney

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.930
is really unprecedented
in Hollywood history.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.270
And it's all because
everybody loves Spider-Man.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.800
And that is amazing.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.457
And I hope it shows in
all the movies as well.

00:01:39.457 --> 00:01:40.890
 Well, you said everyone
loves Spider-Man.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.450
What makes him so
lovable and relatable?

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.820
 I think that was
the genius of what

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.770
Steve Ditko and Stan Lee
did all those years ago

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.150
was they made him us.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.960
They made him
flawed and related.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.160
And again, here he is in this
giant, anticipated movie that

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.680
may or may not have
consequences for the Multiverse,

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.960
but Peter Parker just
wants to go to college.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.700
Peter Parker just wants
to graduate high school.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.610
That's it.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:05.220
And you want to root
for that person.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.810
 Kevin, thank you so much.
Enjoy the movie.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.170
Thank you so much.
Have a good night.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:08.970
Thank you.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:12.320
[MUSIC PLAYING]

